---
import "../../styles/global.css";

export function getStaticPaths() {
  const project = {
    slug: "multibody-systems",
    title: "Multibody Systems",
    summary: "A general 2D multibody framework that numerically integrates the motion of systems connected by spring-dampers and rigid rods under gravity.",
  };
  return [{ params: { slug: project.slug }, props: { project } }];
}

const { project } = Astro.props;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="description" content={project.summary} />
    <title>{project.title} — Manuel Delgado Portfolio</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="case-study">
      <header class="case-header"><a href="/Web-Portofolio/#projects">← Projects</a><a href="/Web-Portofolio/">Manuel Delgado Portfolio</a></header>
      <section class="case-hero"><p class="section-index">MULTIBODY SYSTEMS</p><h1>Constraint Physics</h1><p>Rigid-rod constraints and the system solved at each simulation timestep.</p></section>
      <article class="constraint-article">
        <section class="constraint-section">
          <p class="section-index">CONSTRAINT KINEMATICS</p>
          <h2>Geometric compatibility</h2>
          <p>A rigid connection is defined by a holonomic constraint.</p>
          <div class="equation"><math display="block"><mi>C</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></div>
          <p>For the normalized rod used here,</p>
          <div class="equation"><math display="block"><mi>C</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></div>
          <p>If the constraint remains satisfied over time, its velocity- and acceleration-level conditions must also vanish.</p>
          <div class="equation"><math display="block"><mi>J</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></div>
          <div class="equation"><math display="block"><mi>J</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>J</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></div>
          <p>Here, <span class="inline-equation"><math><mi>J</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></span> is the constraint Jacobian. The acceleration condition keeps the motion compatible with the geometry of the rigid connection.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="constraint-section">
          <p class="section-index">CONSTRAINT FORCES</p>
          <h2>Solving for the reaction force</h2>
          <p>The equations of motion include the constraint force through the Lagrange multiplier λ.</p>
          <div class="equation"><math display="block"><mi>M</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mtext>ext</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>λ</mi></math></div>
          <div class="equation"><math display="block"><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>Q</mi><mtext>ext</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>λ</mi></math></div>
          <p>Substituting this acceleration into the compatibility condition gives</p>
          <div class="equation"><math display="block"><mi>J</mi><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>J</mi><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>Q</mi><mtext>ext</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>J</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></math></div>
        </section>

        <section class="constraint-section solver-section">
          <p class="section-index">CONSTRAINT SOLVER</p>
          <h2>A linear system at each timestep</h2>
          <div class="equation"><math display="block"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>J</mi><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>J</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></math></div>
          <div class="equation"><math display="block"><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>J</mi><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>Q</mi><mtext>ext</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>J</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></math></div>
          <div class="equation equation-final"><math display="block"><mi>A</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi></math></div>
          <p>For the normalized rod constraint, each component of λ has units of force. It represents the axial tension or compression required to maintain the rigid connection.</p>
          <div class="constraint-chain" aria-label="Constraint solver derivation">
            <math display="block"><mi>C</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace width="1em"/><mo>→</mo><mspace width="1em"/><mi>J</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace width="1em"/><mo>→</mo><mspace width="1em"/><mi>J</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>J</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace width="1em"/><mo>→</mo><mspace width="1em"/><mi>A</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi></math>
          </div>
        </section>
      </article>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
